course: dictionary
lesson: 16178
title: Roman numeral XVI
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Romans wrote numbers with letters. I means 1, V means 5 and X means 10. XVI is a Roman numeral, and you can work out its value by adding the letters together.
explain: The bigger letter comes first, so you add. XVI is X + V + I = 10 + 5 + 1 = 16. Read from left to right: 10, then 5 more, then 1 more.
explain: «We are reading Chapter XVI before bed.» Chapter XVI is chapter 16. Roman numbers like this are used in book chapters, on clocks and in the names of kings, so it is useful to know how to read them.
fact: XVI is the Roman numeral for 16.
fact: I means 1, V means 5 and X means 10.
fact: «Louis XVI» means Louis the Sixteenth, a king of France.
fact: Louis XVI was king of France at the time of the French Revolution.
exercise: «We are reading Chapter XVI before bed.» What number is XVI? | 17 | 6 | 15 | *16
exercise: Add up the letters in XVI: X + V + I. What is the total? | *16 | 14 | 26 | 6
exercise: «Louis XVI was a king of France.» What does Louis XVI mean? | *Louis the Sixteenth | Louis the Sixth | Louis the One Hundred | Louis the Sixty
test: What is 10 + 5 + 1, written as a Roman numeral? | XV | XVII | *XVI | VXI
test: In Roman numerals, what does V stand for? | 50 | *5 | 1 | 10
exam: Which Roman numeral means 16? | XVII | *XVI | XIV | VXI
